kind: fix
upstream: not yet reported to V-HACD (which its author considers deprecated).

`VoxelHull::m_voxelHullCount` is a plain static that every decomposition
increments, so two decompositions running at once race on it, which is
undefined. Nothing reads its value, so an atomic makes it race-free without a
lock.

Reproduced 2026-11-01 with clang -fsanitize=thread: two threads each
decomposing a cube on their own instance (resolution 20,000, no worker pool):
  pristine:  WARNING: ThreadSanitizer: data race
  patched:   clean
Covered by: tests/test_threads.py (vhacd.decompose on 8 threads), which
`uv run scripts tsan` runs under TSan.

--- a/include/VHACD.h
+++ b/include/VHACD.h
@@ -5965,12 +5965,14 @@
     std::unordered_map<uint32_t, uint32_t>      m_voxelIndexMap; // Maps from a voxel coordinate space into a vertex index space
     std::vector<VHACD::Vertex>                  m_vertices;
     std::vector<VHACD::Triangle>                m_indices;
-    static uint32_t                             m_voxelHullCount;
+    // trimkit (vendor/patches/vhacd-atomic-hull-counter.patch): atomic, as concurrent
+    // decompositions all increment it (a data race under TSan); its value is never read
+    static std::atomic<uint32_t>                m_voxelHullCount;
     IVHACD::Parameters                          m_params;
     VHACDCallbacks*                             m_callbacks{ nullptr };
 };
 
-uint32_t VoxelHull::m_voxelHullCount = 0;
+std::atomic<uint32_t> VoxelHull::m_voxelHullCount{0};
 
 VoxelHull::VoxelHull(const VoxelHull& parent,
                      SplitAxis axis,
